--- IR --->
// the empty value of each shape, at an argument the parser could not type. a wrapped `T?` is a cleared
// tag - `zeroinitializer` over `{ i1 __has, T }` - and the free shape is a null handle. before the binding
// the null had no type at all and every one of these was a `ptr null`, which for the two wrapped
// parameters is not even the right *width*, let alone the right value
//
// `MQ` is the nullable level and what follows it is the payload's own mangling, so a wrapped one reads
// `MQMLPi` where a class handle - whose `?` is a flag on one address rather than a pair - reads `MQLC4Node`
CHECK: define i32 @main(
CHECK: call i32 @_tag_ofZZMQMLPi(%eco.optional.MLPi zeroinitializer)
CHECK: call i32 @_x_ofZZMQMLC5Point(%eco.optional.MLC5Point zeroinitializer)
CHECK: call i32 @_node_tagZZMQLC4Node(ptr null)
// a member call's written null is argument 1, behind the receiver, and takes the same route
CHECK: call i32 @_M5Store_readingZZMRBMLC5StoreZMQMLPi(ptr %s, %eco.optional.MLPi zeroinitializer)
// and a constructor's, which is where this was first seen to crash
CHECK: call void @_RowZZMQMLPi(ptr noalias sret(%Row)
CHECK: %eco.optional.MLPi zeroinitializer)
